# Local demo catalogue seed

Single orchestrator that clears local TEC data, seeds a **curated catalogue** of cases
(PCN, batch, exception) in known states using only existing `bin/` scripts, then
regenerates a **design docs** page so designers can open each case in Manage Cases with an
explanation of what that case demonstrates.

Status: **implemented** — run `./bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh` after `bootWithCCD` is up.
See [Local bin scripts](/local-scripts.html) for the primitives it composes.

## Goals

1. One command to reset and re-seed a predictable local demo set after `bootWithCCD` is up.
2. Compose existing scripts only — no new CCD/API curl logic in the orchestrator.
3. Keep scenario **prose** in git; keep live **case references** out of git (they change every run).
4. Surface links + explanations on the design docs site for local use
   ([http://localhost:4567](http://localhost:4567)).

## Non-goals

- Seeding every `CaseState` × authority combination (catalogue stays curated).
- Committing ExUI URLs with case refs to `main` / GitHub Pages (always stale for other machines).
- Replacing individual create/link/state scripts — those remain the public primitives.

## Architecture

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  clear["bin/clear-tec-cases.sh --yes"]
  orch["bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh"]
  create["create-tec-batch / create-tec-case / create-tec-exception-case"]
  mutate["set-case-state / transition-to-case-issued / apply-warrant-authorisation / link-pcn-to-batch / …"]
  partial["design_docs … _local_demo_case_links.html.erb gitignored"]
  page["design_docs … local-demo-cases.html.md.erb committed"]
  exui["Manage Cases :3000"]

  orch --> clear
  orch --> create
  create --> mutate
  orch -->|"writes refs + explanations"| partial
  page -->|"includes partial or fallback"| partial
  partial -->|"case-details URLs"| exui
```

| Piece | Role | In git? |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh` | Orchestrator: clear → recipes → write partial | Yes |
| Scenario catalogue (data inside the script) | Stable ids, titles, explanations, recipe steps | Yes |
| `design_docs/source/local-demo-cases.html.md.erb` | Intro, how to run, warning that links are local-only | Yes |
| `design_docs/source/partials/_local_demo_case_links.html.erb` | Generated table of links | **No** (gitignored) |
| `bin/.demo-catalogue.json` | Machine-readable dump of last seed | **No** (gitignored) |

### Why split prose from refs

CCD case references are allocated at create time. After every
`clear-tec-cases` + re-seed they change. Committing them would break links for other developers
and for any published design docs. The committed page explains the catalogue; the generated
partial holds only the current machine’s refs.

### How create-script output is consumed

Create scripts already print JSON with `caseReference` on **stdout** and progress on **stderr**.
The orchestrator captures refs with `jq`:

```bash
BATCH_REF="$(./bin/create-tec-batch.sh westminster | jq -r '.caseReference')"
PCN_REF="$(./bin/create-tec-case.sh "${BATCH_REF}" | jq -r '.caseReference')"
```

Passing a batch ref into `create-tec-case.sh` / `create-tec-cases.sh` links after create
(see [Local bin scripts — Link and transition](/local-scripts.html#link-and-transition)).
No separate link step is required for that path.

ExUI deep link shape (nav proxy, not `:3002`):

```text
http://localhost:3000/cases/case-details/<caseReference>
```

## Scenario catalogue

Curated set — enough for design review of Tasks / Case details / Linked Cases, not a full
state matrix. Prefer **real lifecycle scripts** where they exist; use
`bin/set-case-state.sh` only for prototype-only PCN states (see
[CCD architecture — States and events](/ccd-architecture.html#states-and-events)).

| Id | Type | Demonstrates | Recipe sketch |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `pcn-pending-case-issued` | `TEC` | Fresh registration, payment pending | `create-tec-case.sh -` (leave default state) |
| `pcn-case-issued` | `TEC` | After registration payment | create → `transition-to-case-issued.sh` |
| `pcn-awaiting-la-oot` | `TEC` | Prototype OOT / LA response Tasks | create → `set-case-state.sh … AWAITING_LA_OOT_RESPONSE` |
| `pcn-warrant-issued` | `TEC` | Warrant authorisation on case | create → `apply-warrant-authorisation.sh` (`STATUS=active`) |
| `pcn-warrant-expired` | `TEC` | Expired warrant | create → `STATUS=expired apply-warrant-authorisation.sh` |
| `pcn-refer-enforcement` | `TEC` | Transfer-request link side-effect | `create-tec-batch.sh … transferRequest` → `create-tec-case.sh "${BATCH_REF}"` |
| `pcn-closed` | `TEC` | Closure-request link side-effect | `create-tec-batch.sh … caseClosureRequests` → create with batch ref |
| `batch-registration-with-pcns` | `TEC_BATCH` + linked `TEC` | Registration batch + Linked Cases | `create-tec-batch.sh` → `CASE_COUNT=n create-tec-cases.sh "${BATCH_REF}"` |
| `batch-queued` | `TEC_BATCH` | Queued for processing | `TARGET_STATE=QUEUED_FOR_PROCESSING create-tec-batch.sh …` |
| `batch-processing-complete` | `TEC_BATCH` | Processing complete | `TARGET_STATE=PROCESSING_COMPLETE create-tec-batch.sh …` |
| `exception-pending-review` | `TEC_EXCEPTION` | Exception review Tasks | `create-tec-exception-case.sh` |

Explanations on the design page are short and aimed at designers: what to look at in ExUI.

When you change which demos exist, update this table so it stays aligned with
`seed_catalogue()` in the script.

## Customising the catalogue

The live catalogue is **not** a separate config file. Edit
`bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh` — specifically the `seed_catalogue()` function.
Each demo is a short **recipe** (calls to existing `bin/*.sh`) followed by a
**`record_entry`** so the case appears on the design docs page.

After any change, re-run with the stack up:

```bash
./bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh
```

That clears (unless `--skip-clear`), recreates cases, and rewrites the generated
partial. Refresh [Local demo cases](http://localhost:4567/local-demo-cases.html).

### `record_entry` fields

```bash
record_entry \
  "<id>" \
  "<title shown on the design page>" \
  "<TEC|TEC_BATCH|TEC_EXCEPTION>" \
  "<state label>" \
  "<caseReference>" \
  "<short explanation for designers>"
```

| Argument | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `id` | Stable slug; becomes HTML anchor `#demo-<id>` on the design page. Prefer kebab-case |
| `title` | Human heading in the table |
| case type | `TEC`, `TEC_BATCH`, or `TEC_EXCEPTION` |
| state | CCD state name (or the value returned by a mutate script) |
| case reference | From `require_ref` / create-script JSON |
| explanation | One or two sentences: what to open in ExUI, not CCD event IDs |

### Helpers already in the script

| Helper | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `require_ref <script> [args…]` | Run a create script; print `caseReference` or exit |
| `state_from_json_cmd <fallback> <script> [args…]` | Run a mutate script that prints JSON; print `.state` (or fallback) |
| `unique_batch_identifier` | New `RAB######` id matching create-batch validation |
| `record_entry …` | Append one row to the in-memory catalogue (later written to the partial) |

Typical PCN patterns:

```bash
# Leave create default (PENDING_CASE_ISSUED)
ref="$(require_ref "${SCRIPT_DIR}/create-tec-case.sh" -)"
record_entry "pcn-pending-case-issued" "…" "TEC" "PENDING_CASE_ISSUED" "${ref}" "…"

# Real lifecycle
ref="$(require_ref "${SCRIPT_DIR}/create-tec-case.sh" -)"
state="$(state_from_json_cmd CASE_ISSUED "${SCRIPT_DIR}/transition-to-case-issued.sh" "${ref}")"
record_entry "pcn-case-issued" "…" "TEC" "${state}" "${ref}" "…"

# Prototype-only state
ref="$(require_ref "${SCRIPT_DIR}/create-tec-case.sh" -)"
state="$(state_from_json_cmd AWAITING_LA_OOT_RESPONSE \
  "${SCRIPT_DIR}/set-case-state.sh" "${ref}" AWAITING_LA_OOT_RESPONSE)"
record_entry "pcn-awaiting-la-oot" "…" "TEC" "${state}" "${ref}" "…"

# Create + link to a batch (side-effects depend on batch type)
BATCH_IDENTIFIER="$(unique_batch_identifier)"
batch_ref="$(require_ref "${SCRIPT_DIR}/create-tec-batch.sh" westminster transferRequest)"
ref="$(require_ref "${SCRIPT_DIR}/create-tec-case.sh" "${batch_ref}")"
record_entry "pcn-refer-enforcement" "…" "TEC" "REFER_FOR_ENFORCEMENT" "${ref}" "…"
```

Pass env into a helper the same way as a normal command:

```bash
state="$(
  STATUS=active state_from_json_cmd WARRANT_AUTHORISATION_ISSUED \
    "${SCRIPT_DIR}/apply-warrant-authorisation.sh" "${ref}"
)"
```

### Add, change, or remove a demo

1. **Change** — edit that block’s recipe and/or `record_entry` title / explanation / state.
2. **Remove** — delete (or comment out) the whole block in `seed_catalogue()`.
3. **Add** — copy a similar block; compose only scripts from
   [Local bin scripts](/local-scripts.html). Call `record_entry` so the row is emitted.
4. Prefer **real lifecycle** scripts (`transition-to-case-issued.sh`,
   `apply-warrant-authorisation.sh`, batch link via create) where they exist; use
   `set-case-state.sh` for prototype-only PCN states.
5. Keep **`id`s stable** if designers bookmark `#demo-…` anchors.
6. Update the [scenario catalogue](#scenario-catalogue) table on this page when the set of demos changes.
7. Do **not** hand-edit `design_docs/source/partials/_local_demo_case_links.html.erb` —
   it is gitignored and overwritten on every seed.

### Light tuning without editing recipes

| Mechanism | Effect |
| --- | --- |
| `REGISTRATION_PCN_COUNT` | PCNs created for `batch-registration-with-pcns` (default `3`) |
| `EXUI_BASE_URL` | Base URL for case links (default `http://localhost:3000`) |
| `DESIGN_DOCS_URL` | Printed at end of the run |
| `TEC_API_URL` | Health check / create APIs (default `http://localhost:4013`) |
| `--skip-clear` / `SKIP_CLEAR=true` | Re-seed without `clear-tec-cases.sh` (refs accumulate; usually avoid) |

```bash
REGISTRATION_PCN_COUNT=5 ./bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh
./bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh --skip-clear
```

### Implementation pitfalls

- **Batch identifiers** must match `^R[A-Z]{2,3}[0-9]{6}$` (use `unique_batch_identifier`, or set
  `BATCH_IDENTIFIER` / `FILE_IDENTIFIER` consistently when overriding).
- **Progress on stderr**, machine data on stdout from create scripts — keep that split so
  `require_ref` / `jq` stay reliable.
- When writing JSON with `jq` and only `--arg` / `--argjson` (no stdin payload), use
  `--null-input` so an interactive TTY does not hang waiting for input.
- Stack must match current source (Definition Store + API). Stale `bootWithCCD` runs can reject
  newer batch types or `CaseState` values — restart with `./bin/restart-boot-with-ccd.sh`.

## Orchestrator behaviour

Script: `bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh`.

```bash
./bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh
./bin/seed-demo-catalogue.sh --skip-clear   # re-seed without wiping
```

1. Require stack up (`TEC_API_URL` /health); fail fast with a clear message.
2. Run `./bin/clear-tec-cases.sh --yes` (unless `--skip-clear`).
3. For each catalogue entry, run the recipe via existing scripts; collect
   `{ id, title, caseType, state, caseReference, url, explanation }`.
4. Write `design_docs/source/partials/_local_demo_case_links.html.erb` (HTML table).
5. Write `bin/.demo-catalogue.json` for debugging.
6. Print to stderr: count created, paths, design docs URL
   `http://localhost:4567/local-demo-cases.html`.

Optional env: `TEC_API_URL`, `EXUI_BASE_URL`, `DESIGN_DOCS_URL`,
`REGISTRATION_PCN_COUNT` (default 3), `SKIP_CLEAR`.

Constraints:

- `set -euo pipefail`; progress on stderr.
- Do not call CCD/HTTP directly — only invoke `bin/*.sh`.
- Batch identifiers match `^R[A-Z]{2,3}[0-9]{6}$`.

